THE COMPLETE ECO OPENING CODE REFERENCE (A00–E99)
All 500 Encyclopaedia of Chess Openings codes, grouped by opening
family, with every numbered variation listed as a sub-entry.
==============================================================================

ABOUT THIS LIST
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The Encyclopaedia of Chess Openings (ECO) is the standard classification
system for chess openings, first published by Chess Informant (1974-1979).
It divides all openings into 5 volumes (A-E), each containing 100 codes
(00-99), for 500 codes total. Each code corresponds to a specific position
reached after a defined sequence of moves.

Structure of this document:
  * Each VOLUME (A-E) is a major division of chess openings.
  * Each MAIN BULLET is a named opening / opening family.
  * Each SUB-BULLET is one specific ECO code (a variation or sub-line)
    within that family, with its defining move sequence.
  * Where a variation has its own traditional name (e.g. 'Poisoned Pawn
    Variation', 'Marshall Attack'), that name is given; otherwise the
    defining move sequence for that ECO code is shown.

Move notation is standard algebraic notation, White then Black per move
number. Long theoretical lines are shown to the point that reliably
identifies the branch; deeper sub-theory continues under the same code.

Sourced from and cross-checked against the Encyclopaedia of Chess
Openings classification as documented on Wikipedia's 'List of ECO
codes' and standard opening references (365chess.com, chessgames.com).

TABLE OF CONTENTS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Volume A: Flank & Irregular Openings (A00–A99)
  Volume B: Semi-Open Games (excl. French) (B00–B99)
